  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">NULL - El Salvador (01-Jan-2014-31-Dec-2016)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Although significant advances have been made in the HIV and AIDS epidemic in El Salvador, they still face many challenges. This Program is a consolidation of the Round 7 and Round 2 HIV grants and is being implemented by 2 Principal Recipients (PR) under dual-track financing. This PR is responsible for the training of health care staff in HIV and AIDS care, treatment and prevention; strengthening of prevention activities focusing on mobile populations and persons deprived of their freedom; training of persons working for municipal councils in the response towards HIV and AIDS; implementing and expanding the mass media campaign; and expansion of voluntary counselling, testing, diagnosis and treatment services. The goal of this Program is to reduce the incidence of HIV and AIDS among populations living in highly vulnerable conditions as well as the social and economic impact of the HIV and AIDS epidemic.</narrative>
  </description>
